                <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white pt-4">1. Mount Airy Forest & Doris Day Dog Park</h2>
                <p>
                    Spanning nearly 1,500 acres, <strong>Mount Airy Forest</strong> is the largest park in the Cincinnati Parks system. It offers miles of shaded hiking trails, wooded valleys, and scenic vistas. 
                </p>
                <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
                    <li><strong>Leashed Trail Walks:</strong> Perfect for structured, high-endurance dog walking. The trails feature natural soil paths with wonderful seasonal foliage. *(Note: Dogs are welcome on all standard park trails on a leash, though they are restricted inside the dedicated Mt. Airy Arboretum to protect rare plant collections).*</li>
                    <li><strong>Doris Day Dog Park:</strong> Located right within the complex at 2970 Westwood Northern Blvd, this fully fenced, enclosed dog park gives friendly dogs a secure place to run off-leash and socialize.</li>
                </ul>

                <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white pt-4">2. Professional Pups Need Reliable Routines</h2>
